&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated as deemed distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $50 million in 2025 and $70 million in 2024 and was included within Other Paid-In Capital on the Comparative Balance Sheet. We will make all necessary adjustments to account balances upon a ruling in Docket No. AC18-220-000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the United States enacted the &amp;#8220;Tax Cuts and Jobs Act&amp;#8221; (&amp;#8220;TCJA &amp;#8221;). The changes in the TCJA are effective for taxation years beginning after December 31, 2017. While the changes are broad and complex, the most significant change is the reduction in the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. We recorded a $233 million decrease to our 2017 deferred income tax liability, a $92 million increase to our 2017 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting increase of $325 million to our regulatory liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;In 2020, as a result of the AGT Stipulation and Agreement Docket RP19-57 (&amp;#8220;Agreement&amp;#8221;), we began amortizing the regulated liability utilizing the reverse South Georgia flowback methodology over the&amp;#160;32.3 year&amp;#160;remaining life of the assets. In 2025, we recorded&amp;#160;an&amp;#160;$14 million decrease to our regulatory liability, a $4 million decrease to our 2025 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $10 million benefit to our 2025 deferred federal tax expense in accordance to the agreement. In 2024, we recorded&amp;#160;an&amp;#160;$14 million decrease to our regulatory liability, a $4 million decrease to our 2024 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $10 million benefit to our 2024 deferred federal tax expense in accordance to the agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;10. Related&amp;#160;Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Related party transactions are conducted in the normal course of business and, unless otherwise noted,&amp;#160;are measured at the exchange amount, which is the amount of consideration established and agreed to&amp;#160;by the related parties.&amp;#160;In the normal course of business, we provide natural gas transportation services to affiliates of Enbridge&amp;#160;and our members. In addition, Enbridge and its affiliates provide management and operating services to&amp;#160;us, pursuant to agreements&amp;#160;entered into&amp;#160;with us. We reimburse Enbridge for the expenses incurred to&amp;#160;provide these services, as well as for other expenses incurred on our behalf.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 13.9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Our transactions with related parties are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
